186138302 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4999" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138302 #edb/ref 1071 "Factor the expression $x^3 - 6x^2 + 9x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138302 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "da0223c6-ff03-55da-992c-d8a1ef3f9aff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138302 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that all of the terms have a common factor of $x.$ To simplify the computation, we can factor out the $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx^3 - 6x^2 + 9x = x(x^2 - 6x + 9)\n$$\n\nThe expression $x^2 - 6x + 9$ is a perfect square trinomial that can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x({x}^{2}-6x+9) & = \\\\ x({x}^{2}-6x+{3}^{2}) & = \\\\ x({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2}) & = \\\\ x(x-3)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138303 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138303 #edb/ref 1071 "Factor the expression $x^3 + x^2 - 2x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138303 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "007b9b7b-5fab-5e50-9598-fc94a9f6edde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138303 #edb/ref 1074 "Note that all of the terms have a common factor of $x.$ To simplify the computation, we can factor out the $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-2x & =x({x}^{2}+x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the polynomial $x^2 + x - 2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x({x}^{2}+x-2) & = \\\\ x(({x}^{2}-x)+(2x-2)) & = \\\\ x(x(x-1)+2(x-1)) & = \\\\ x(x+2)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138386 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138386 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138386 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186139161 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138386 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186139162 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138386 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186530489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138386 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186530528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138386 #edb/ref 1039 "Factoring Using Common Factors and Differences o